{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const PUNCTUATION_CODE_MAP: Record<string, string>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/constants.ts#L277","children":[{"type":"text","value":"constants.ts:277"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyboardEvent.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values for punctuation keys to their canonical characters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On macOS, holding the Option (Alt) key transforms punctuation keys into special characters\n(e.g., Option+Minus → en-dash '–'), causing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.key"},{"type":"text","value":" to differ from the expected character.\nHowever, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" still reports the physical key (e.g., 'Minus'). This map enables\nfalling back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" for punctuation keys, similar to the existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Key*"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Digit*"},{"type":"text","value":"\nfallbacks for letters and digits."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst PUNCTUATION_CODE_MAP: Record<string, string>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [constants.ts:277](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/constants.ts#L277)\n\nMaps `KeyboardEvent.code` values for punctuation keys to their canonical characters.\n\nOn macOS, holding the Option (Alt) key transforms punctuation keys into special characters\n(e.g., Option+Minus → en-dash '–'), causing `event.key` to differ from the expected character.\nHowever, `event.code` still reports the physical key (e.g., 'Minus'). This map enables\nfalling back to `event.code` for punctuation keys, similar to the existing `Key*`/`Digit*`\nfallbacks for letters and digits.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: PUNCTUATION_CODE_MAP\ntitle: PUNCTUATION_CODE_MAP\n---\n\n```ts\nconst PUNCTUATION_CODE_MAP: Record<string, string>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [constants.ts:277](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/constants.ts#L277)\n\nMaps `KeyboardEvent.code` values for punctuation keys to their canonical characters.\n\nOn macOS, holding the Option (Alt) key transforms punctuation keys into special characters\n(e.g., Option+Minus → en-dash '–'), causing `event.key` to differ from the expected character.\nHowever, `event.code` still reports the physical key (e.g., 'Minus'). This map enables\nfalling back to `event.code` for punctuation keys, similar to the existing `Key*`/`Digit*`\nfallbacks for letters and digits.\n"}
